-- title:
--   Minimal primes as j₀-fixing translates of the Tate kernel
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and an auxiliary prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity $\xi$ for which some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$; let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$, and let $K \subseteq L((X))$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\ell_g$, $M'$ invertible, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is that of the $j$-function, assumed nonzero. Assume the variable-change and base-change equivariance hypotheses `hℓ`, `hM`, `hL` for $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-points, prime-power cyclic kernel polynomials and `inLineMulPoly` divisibility, group laws $\mathcal{G}$ that are chord-tangent with origin as identity, a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for Drinfeld bases of level $q$ that is a section transport, and the existence of graded homomorphisms realising variable changes (`hVC`) and coefficient maps (`hCO`) on projective models, all summarised here. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the level moduli datum of `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q …`, with $B_0$ of finite type over $A$, and let $x$ be a $K$-point whose $j$-invariant has Laurent expansion `jqNModC L q`. Suppose $A[P_0.j_0]$ is a domain and that every $k \in K$ is a ratio $\mathrm{classify}_x(a)/\mathrm{classify}_x(b)$ of two values of the classifying map of $x$. Then every minimal prime $\mathfrak{p}$ of $(0) \subseteq B_0$ is of the form $e^{-1}(\ker \mathrm{classify}_x)$ for some $A$-algebra automorphism $e$ of $B_0$ fixing the universal $j$-invariant $\mathrm{jOf}(P_0.\mathrm{univ})$.
--
--   This is the orbit-exhaustion step for the $H_1$ level structure: the irreducible components of the fine moduli ring $B_0$ are exactly the automorphic translates, by automorphisms fixing the universal $j$-invariant, of the component cut out by the Tate point $x$. It feeds the combined statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.ker_classify_mem_minimalPrimes_and_forall_exists_algEquiv_comap_eq_rigidDataH1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.ker_classify_mem_minimalPrimes_and_forall_exists_algEquiv_comap_eq_rigidDataH1Pow), which is used to control the components, and hence the fields of definition, of the moduli scheme of level $\Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ together with a Drinfeld basis of level $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_Diamond_forall_exists_algEquiv_comap_ker_classify_eq_of_dense_rigidDataH1Pow.lean

